================================================================================
 WHAT THIS PROJECT IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT
================================================================================

Scan-to-Text is a FILING AND TRANSCRIPTION LAYER. What we built is the pipeline
that watches a scanner folder, splits what arrives into documents, finds whose
document each one is, and writes a literal transcription into the right
folder - not the models that recognise the text.

Layout analysis and table structure are performed by Docling (IBM Research and
the Docling project). Character recognition is performed by RapidOCR running
PaddleOCR models. Both are third-party components. We are not their authors and
claim no authorship over them.

What is ours: the folder watcher, the locks between workstations, the reading
rules that work on text ALREADY recognised (patient labels, dates and their
roles, document categories, page segmentation, the cleaning of page furniture),
the output tree, the manifest, and the safety rails around patient data.

